    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76-a8">

                <pb facs="0235" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg107"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No. 387.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to President
                            Zaldivar</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 12,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>To-day I have addressed you a telegram acknowledging the receipt of yours of the
                    10th and 11th instant. I have now the pleasure to acknowledge the receipt of
                    yours of to-day, announcing that peace has been signed between Salvador,
                    Nicaragua, Costa Rica, and Honduras. In view of the disposition of the present
                    Government of Guatemala, which inspires the necessary confidence, and the good
                    intentions you have manifested, I have no doubt that the two Governments will
                    come to an honorable and satisfactory settlement. I believe the aid of the
                    diplomatic corps can be depended upon. I assure, you that I shall do everything
                    in my power to that end.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENRY C. HALL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
